  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1155 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nHot and dry conditions this weekend are expected to persist \nthrough much of next week, as high pressure remains steadfast \nover the region through the long term forecast. There remains\nlittle to no change in the high and low temperatures expected\nthrough much of the long term forecast. Afternoon highs are\nexpected to reach into the mid 90s and up to around 104 degrees, \nand overnight lows in the 70s. The warmest temperatures are \nexpected across the Big Country and northern portions of the \nConcho Valley and Heartland. \n\nSouth winds will continue and remain breezy through Saturday \nevening, then decrease slightly over the remainder of the weekend \nand into mid next week as the surface pressure gradient weakens to\nsome extent. Breezy southerly winds are forecast to pick back up \nfor the second half of next week. Given the hot and drier \nconditions, along with some breezy southerly winds, there remains \nsome fire weather concerns over this weekend.",
